I sit near the sea at Marine Drive.
The water is vast and blue.
Many people walk on the road.
Some people come from the left.
Some people come from the right.
I look at the long road.
That road is curved.
I remember my journey today.
I make a map of the city in my mind.
The fruit vendor said— "Turn left."
The elderly shopkeeper said— "Turn right."
He said again— "Go straight towards the sea."
I followed all the directions.
Now I know this part of Mumbai.
The route to my home is also clear.
A cool wind blows here.
I sit peacefully.
I just watch the water.
